  "metaDescription": "Search teams continue recovery efforts at PT Fonusa Agung Mulia in Cikande as authorities launch an investigation into the deadly candy factory fire.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Search and rescue teams have recovered 26 sets of remains, while approximately 28 to 30 workers remain reported missing.",
    "Authorities have upgraded the factory fire case to a formal investigation due to suspected safety standard violations.",
    "The factory management and national insurance agencies are processing compensation and social security benefits for the affected workers and families."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "A major fire recently devastated a candy manufacturing plant operated by PT Fonusa Agung Mulia in Cikande, Banten. Search efforts are ongoing as rescue teams clear the site to locate remaining victims. Authorities have officially launched a criminal investigation into the incident, citing potential failures in workplace health and safety (K3) regulations. While 16 victims have been identified so far, families continue to wait for news of missing loved ones. In response to the tragedy, the company has visited the families of employees affected by the disaster, and government representatives have urged a thorough investigation into the protection of workers' rights. Furthermore, BPJS Ketenagakerjaan has begun processing insurance claims and financial assistance for the heirs of the victims, while labor unions have demanded significant compensation for those harmed by the incident.",
